---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <meta name="description" content={description} />
    <meta name="theme-color" content="#f7f7f8" />
    <meta property="og:title" content={title} />
    <meta property="og:description" content={description} />
    <meta property="og:type" content="website" />
    <meta property="og:site_name" content={siteName} />
    <meta name="twitter:card" content="summary" />
    <meta name="twitter:title" content={title} />
    <meta name="twitter:description" content={description} />
    <title>{title}</title>
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com" />
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin />
    <link
      rel="stylesheet"
      href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Xanh+Mono:ital@0;1&display=swap"
    />
    <link rel="icon" type="image/x-icon" href="/favicon.ico" />
    <link rel="icon" type="image/png" sizes="32x32" href="/favicon-32.png" />
    <link rel="icon" type="image/png" sizes="16x16" href="/favicon-16.png" />
    <link rel="apple-touch-icon" sizes="180x180" href="/apple-touch-icon.png" />
    <style is:global>
      * {
        box-sizing: border-box;
        margin: 0;
        padding: 0;
      }

      html {
        background: #f7f7f8;
      }

      body {
        min-height: 100vh;
        padding: 40px;
        color: #111111;
        background: #f7f7f8;
        font-family: ui-monospace, "SF Mono", SFMono-Regular, Menlo, Monaco, "Cascadia Mono",
          Consolas, "Liberation Mono", monospace;
        font-size: 12px;
        line-height: 20px;
      }

      main {
        display: grid;
        gap: 20px;
        justify-items: start;
      }

      .letter,
      .model,
      .members {
        display: grid;
        gap: 20px;
      }

      .member-list {
        list-style: disc;
        padding-left: 2ch;
      }

      .para {
        max-width: 72ch;
      }

      .sep,
      h1,
      .label {
        font-size: inherit;
        font-weight: 400;
      }

      h1,
      .label {
        font-family: "Xanh Mono", ui-monospace, Menlo, monospace;
        font-size: 15px;
        letter-spacing: 0.04em;
      }

      a {
        color: #0000ee;
      }

      a:visited {
        color: #551a8b;
      }

      .cursor {
        animation: blink 1s step-end infinite;
      }

      @keyframes blink {
        50% {
          opacity: 0;
        }
      }

      .signature {
        width: 280px;
        max-width: 100%;
        height: auto;
        margin-top: 20px;
        overflow: visible;
      }

      .sig-ink path {
        fill: #111111;
      }

      /* Sits a hair below the ink so the writing leaves an indent behind it. */
      .sig-ghost {
        transform: translate(0.6px, 1.3px);
      }

      .sig-ghost path {
        fill: #dcdce0;
      }

      /* Sweeps the soft-edged mask across the signature, left to right. */
      .sig-wipe {
        transform: translateX(-25px);
        animation: sig-write 2.2s cubic-bezier(0.36, 0.1, 0.28, 1) 0.4s forwards;
      }

      @keyframes sig-write {
        to {
          transform: translateX(215px);
        }
      }

      @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
        .cursor {
          animation: none;
        }

        .sig-wipe {
          animation: none;
          transform: translateX(215px);
        }
      }

      @media (max-width: 600px) {
        body {
          padding: 20px;
        }
      }
    </style>
  </head>
  <body>
    <main>
      <h1>MODERN FABER <span class="cursor" aria-hidden="true">_</span></h1>

      <p class="sep" aria-hidden="true">* * *</p>

      <section class="letter" aria-label="To the fabers">
        <p class="label">TO THE FABERS:</p>
        <p class="para">
          Faber is an old word for a maker &mdash; the smith at the forge, the carpenter at the
          bench, the hand that shapes raw material into something that did not exist before.
          <em>Homo faber</em>: the one who makes. There have never been fewer. Not because people
          stopped wanting to make things, but because talking about making became easier than
          making &mdash; the feed rewards the announcement, not the object, and whole rooms fill
          with people circling the work they say they want to do.
        </p>
        <p class="para">
          Modern Faber is a room for the ones who still make. One rule holds it together: come
          back every week with something real, and say what you changed. There is no audience
          here, no applause &mdash; only other fabers paying attention to the details you almost
          skipped. That attention costs something. It is meant to. Keep the rhythm long enough
          and you are left with a body of work, a sharper eye, and the few people you actually
          want beside you at the bench.
        </p>
      </section>

      <p class="sep" aria-hidden="true">* * *</p>

      <section class="model" aria-labelledby="model-heading">
        <p class="label" id="model-heading">HOW WE OPERATE:</p>
        <p class="para">
          <strong>HIGH TRUST, HIGH SIGNAL COMMUNITY.</strong> The commons is open to anyone with
          a serious question. The member room is not &mdash; you get in on the work you share and
          the answers you give, and no one gets in without at least five members agreeing to it.
          Titles count for nothing here. The work counts for everything.
        </p>
        <p class="para">
          <strong>RICH, DENSE MEETUPS.</strong> Three or four people to a table, never more.
          Tables are matched at random &mdash; seven signups become one table of three and one of
          four. Every conversation should be dense enough that each person leaves holding
          something they could not have reached alone.
        </p>
      </section>

      <p class="sep" aria-hidden="true">* * *</p>

      <section class="members" aria-labelledby="members-heading">
        <p class="label" id="members-heading">MEMBERS:</p>
        <ul class="member-list">
          <li class="para">
            John J. &mdash; Co-founder at
            <a href="https://fastrepl.com/">Fastrepl</a> (YC S25).
          </li>
          <li class="para">
            Chanhee L. &mdash; Co-founder at
            <a href="https://aside.com/">Aside</a> (YC F25).
          </li>
          <li class="para">
            Jay S. &mdash; Research engineer at
            <a href="https://www.cartesia.ai/">Cartesia AI</a>; formerly co-founded
            <a href="https://nari-labs.com/">Nari Labs</a> (YC F25).
          </li>
          <li class="para">
            Sunghyun C. &mdash; Research engineer at
            <a href="https://www.twelvelabs.io/">Twelve Labs</a>.
          </li>
          <li class="para">
            <strong>You?</strong> &mdash; Email your best work to
            <a href={inquiryEmailUrl}>{inquiryEmailAddress}</a> and say why you want in.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <svg class="signature" viewBox="17 55.4 186 49" role="img" aria-label="Signed, Modern Faber">
        <defs>
          <linearGradient id="sig-wipe-gradient" x1="0" y1="0" x2="1" y2="0">
            <stop offset="0" stop-color="#ffffff" />
            <stop offset="0.9" stop-color="#ffffff" />
            <stop offset="1" stop-color="#000000" />
          </linearGradient>
          <mask id="sig-wipe-mask" maskUnits="userSpaceOnUse" x="10" y="50" width="210" height="60">
            <rect
              class="sig-wipe"
              x="-420"
              y="50"
              width="460"
              height="60"
              fill="url(#sig-wipe-gradient)"
            />
          </mask>
        </defs>
        <g mask="url(#sig-wipe-mask)">
          <g class="sig-ghost" aria-hidden="true">
            {signaturePaths.map((d) => <path d={d} />)}
          </g>
          <g class="sig-ink">
            {signaturePaths.map((d) => <path d={d} />)}
          </g>
        </g>
      </svg>
    </main>
  </body>
</html>
